  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000121935,
      "SummaryText": "Conecuh Sausage, Andalusia, Alabama has a new state of the art plant that uses anhydrous ammonia as a refrigerant.  The plant will be subject to RMP and PSM regulations.  The plant will become operational in July 2025.  The plant will employ an estimated 130 people.  The system will have an estimated 15000 pounds of NH3 on an estimated date of June 16, 2025.  The facility has developed a comprehensive RMP/PSM Program to protect employees and the surrounding community from a catastrophic ammonia release.  The RMP/PSM program overview:  Employee involvement and management systems, process safety information, process hazard analyses, standard operating procedures, training (initial and on-going), contractor qualification, pre start-up safety review, mechanical integrity for the ammonia system components, safe work/hot work policy and procedure, management of change to the ammonia system, emergency planning with emphasis on coordination, drills, training and safe evacuation of the facility, incident investigation, trade secrets and compliance audits to ensure the RMP/PSM program has been implemented and on-going and is effective at the facility. of the  and trade secrets.  The facility is a evacuation only facility.  Ammonia detectors are positioned to detect, signal alarms and shutdown systems as needed. In addition, Emergency stop buttons and ventilation controls are installed outside the engine room.  Planned changes to improve safety include training with employees, and the local fire department after the plant is operational."
    }
  ]
